hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"921","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb, on the authority of Abu Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Sneezing is from God, and yawning is from Satan, so if one of you yawns, do not say: Ha, for Satan laughs in \His stomach\"""""
"922","Al-San’ani Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, we told us Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, we told us Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God loves sneezing, and hates yawning. If any of you does not say: Ah, Ah, for Satan laughs at him, or he said: He plays with him."
